00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:31.310
Ow!

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:35.520
We can't let a first year
like you take all the glory!

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.600
Hey, could you hold back?

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:40.270
Haijima's changing up his playing style.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:42.940
He's actually following up
on spikes and also digging...

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:47.310
Looks like Haijima's
pretty good on defense, too.

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:48.600
Yes.

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:53.690
But if possible, he'd like to avoid receives.

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:57.060
He's not going to be able to set up
the attacks as the setter.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:58.850
But...

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:00.900
Even then...

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:02.520
Haijima!

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:07.190
But if Kuroba's going to score anyway,
we just need to get the ball up!

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:10.520
I sli--

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.310
Aoki- <i>senpai</i> ...

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:26.520
Don't just use brute force.
Try using your brain, you simpleton.

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:31.600
Securing a point doesn't mean
you need to smash the ball.

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:36.400
You can feint or touch. If you get
the ball over, it's all the same.

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:39.980
Come on. Quit looking so pathetic here.

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:43.310
If you're going to go sit,
go sit down on the bench.

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:54.060
Oda- <i>senpai</i> ...

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:55.440
You worked hard.

00:15:55.440 --> 00:16:00.440
That's plenty. We can win.
Sorry, but I'm gonna take the glory here.

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:58.520
Seiin

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:58.520
Ikeda Biz

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:01.940
Sure. It's all yours...

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:06.810
Hey, come on. I'm kidding.
You're definitely the hero of this set.

00:16:08.810 --> 00:16:10.600
All right, we're taking this set!

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:11.650
Yeah!

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:19.440
Was it wrong, or was it right...

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:25.980
Were you waiting for Haijima
to put himself on the line?

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:33.060
If Haijima was stubborn and didn't
change up his play style and we lost...

00:16:33.060 --> 00:16:35.980
...we would've been doomed.

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:44.400
It's rare that you're actually ever doomed.

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:48.480
I'm sure you kids don't understand that yet.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.270
Come on. Cheer them on.

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:52.690
One more!

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:58.020
Yeah!

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:02.690
One more! Don't let up until we win this thing!

00:17:02.690 --> 00:17:03.810
Yeah!

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:13.230
First years! Hey!

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:14.940
First years!

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:18.100
Yesh?

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:21.730
The bus is leaving at 15 after.
We're leaving without you if you're late.

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:24.020
Got it. I'll be right there.

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:30.150
We won...

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:36.480
Yeah!

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:39.980
We actually won...

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:46.350
Haijima, you heard him. The bus is coming.

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:49.400
Hello?

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:52.520
Haijima, you okay?

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:54.810
We've got two games tomorrow...

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:56.560
I see.

00:17:56.560 --> 00:17:58.600
We get to play two games.

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:00.650
I can't wait until tomorrow.

00:18:00.650 --> 00:18:03.400
You really do love to play, don't you?

00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:07.400
Well, where else am I going
to see your killer plays?

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:09.060
You should do that all the time.

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:12.770
That second set...

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:14.900
That first attack from the back...

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:19.020
I got goosebumps.

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:23.150
R-Right... I-I see.

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:25.190
Yeah.

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:29.650
You didn't have that much fun
at today's game, did you?

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:32.100
Well, there was that combo miss.

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:35.480
You had to give up being a setter to do defense.

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:38.230
If something's wrong, we just need to fix it.

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:40.980
You were super annoyed.

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:43.770
I didn't want things to end today.

00:18:43.770 --> 00:18:46.060
I want to win... with this team.

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:50.400
I want to win more with Seiin.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:55.690
You need to say things like that
in front of the others more.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:59.850
And that's why... I'll do whatever
it takes to connect to tomorrow.

00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:03.600
As long as the game is still going,
we can always turn things around.

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:07.190
There's still so much
I want to do with everyone...

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:09.900
When I think about this at night,

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:12.940
I can't stop thinking about
the possibilities, and I can't sleep.

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:14.150
You're so obsessed.

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:15.980
I know.

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:20.440
Just so you know, I'm not
going to back you up for life.

00:19:20.440 --> 00:19:22.940
I don't need you to. But...

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:24.060
But?

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:26.850
I want us to be on the same team...

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:30.270
So I can keep seeing that
back attack over and over again.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:34.850
And I'm always going to be
the one to set that ball to you.

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:39.810
I-I can show you that as many times as you want.

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:43.650
Anytime, anyplace!

00:19:43.940 --> 00:19:49.560
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:19:51.150 --> 00:19:56.810
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:05.650
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:09.690
<i>The azure world smiles upon me</i>

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:22.020
<i>The knife made up of words from my friend</i>

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:28.940
<i>Still lingers inside my head today</i>

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:35.100
<i>You glared up at the clouds high in the sky</i>

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:41.600
<i>And near your house, the horizon undulated</i>

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:49.060
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:56.190
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:05.100
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:13.270
<i>The azure world stabs me strongly in the back</i>

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:17.580
9/28 Tournament Day 2

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:21.630
Round 4 - Match 2

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:30.600
Seiin High School Wins

00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:32.650
Thank you!

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:35.850
Advance to Play-offs

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:43.100
Aoki- <i>senpai</i> and you were killing it today.

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:44.940
Of course. We fixed our mistakes.

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:47.770
And they decided to not pay attention to Aoki

00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:50.560
after seeing him in yesterday's game.

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:52.440
Of course we'd use that to our advantage.

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:55.190
You used your mistake yesterday against them?

00:21:55.190 --> 00:21:57.900
Man, I'm glad you're on our team.

00:21:58.940 --> 00:22:01.480
Isn't volleyball fun?

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:03.270
Where'd that come from?

00:22:09.100 --> 00:22:10.650
Fukuho...

00:22:10.650 --> 00:22:13.900
Hey, you guys made it.

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:18.100
Glad I didn't waste my time
waiting for you guys, Oda.

00:22:20.020 --> 00:22:21.270
Kuroba!

00:22:21.270 --> 00:22:22.520
Huh?!

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:27.740
"Nanafu Seiin"

00:22:33.440 --> 00:22:34.520
Y-You...

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:52.520
You better not regret that, Yuni Kuroba.

00:22:57.900 --> 00:23:01.230
I'm serious. You better not regret that.
